{"tool_name":"tripoint","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"TriPOINT","home":"https://github.uconn.edu/ajt06004/TriPOINT","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Software tool to prioritize important genes in pathways and their non-coding regulators.","addition_date":"2019-07-04T15:20:34Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:07:14.942480Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Desktop application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:TriPOINT","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Asa Thibodeau","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://github.uconn.edu/ajt06004"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.uconn.edu/ajt06004/TriPOINT/blob/master/README.md"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.uconn.edu/ajt06004/TriPOINT/blob/master/UserManual.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Differential gene expression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3223"},{"term":"Enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3501"},{"term":"Expression profile pathway mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0533"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"TriPOINT","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bty998","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: Current approaches for pathway analyses focus on representing gene expression levels on graph representations of pathways and conducting pathway enrichment among differentially expressed genes. However, gene expression levels by themselves do not reflect the overall picture as non-coding factors play an important role to regulate gene expression. To incorporate these non-coding factors into pathway analyses and to systematically prioritize genes in a pathway we introduce a new software: Triangulation of Perturbation Origins and Identification of Non-Coding Targets. Triangulation of Perturbation Origins and Identification of Non-Coding Targets is a pathway analysis tool, implemented in Java that identifies the significance of a gene under a condition (e.g. a disease phenotype) by studying graph representations of pathways, analyzing upstream and downstream gene interactions and integrating non-coding regions that may be regulating gene expression levels. Availability and implementation: The TriPOINT open source software is freely available at https://github.uconn.edu/ajt06004/TriPOINT under the GPL v3.0 license. Supplementary information: Supplementary data are available at Bioinformatics online.","authors":[{"name":"Shin D.-G."},{"name":"Thibodeau A."}],"date":"2019-08-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"TriPOINT: A software tool to prioritize important genes in pathways and their non-coding regulators"},"pmcid":"PMC6662310","pmid":"30566622","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Functional, regulatory and non-coding RNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0659"},{"term":"Gene regulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0204"},{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"TriPOINT","home":"https://bio.tools/TriPOINT","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Software tool to prioritize important genes in pathways and their non-coding regulators.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:tripoint/app/github.uconn.edu","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"packages":true,"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true,"manual":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":0,"citations":[],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bty998","pmcid":"PMC6662310","pmid":"30566622","ref_count":33,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"